	Crow: I am your Father, child. Your long lost Brothers.
	Crow: I'm your buried little Sister, your Best Friend and your Lover. 
	Crow: I am the Pup you lost when you were four. The Deer Carcass you saw on the side of the road when you were ten. 
	Crow: Most of all, I am your Mother. The Mother of all things, and of all beings. 
	Crow: And I am here to make you mine now, mind and flesh.
